  <section class="team-preview team-preview--dark" id="board">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="team-preview__header">
        <span class="team-preview__eyebrow">Leadership</span>
        <h2 class="team-preview__heading">Board of Directors</h2>
        <p class="team-preview__text">Our volunteer board provides strategic oversight and ensures the Foundation fulfills its mission to strengthen Teton Valley through the power of generosity.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="team-preview__grid">
        <div class="team-preview__card" role="button" tabindex="0" data-bio="Scott moved to Jackson Hole 45 years ago where he worked first as a land surveyor then started his own land consulting business in 1986 with his wife Lisa. Pierson Land Works opened their office on Little Street in Driggs in 2007, which deepened his appreciation for Teton Valley.||Lisa worked for 20 years flying in and out of the Driggs Airport. Scott and Lisa were finally able to buy a home in Alta in 2017. They both retired in 2020. Now they keep busy with skiing, hiking, biking and Lisa's flying.||Scott is a member of the Alta Solid Waste District and Advisory Board, the Bank of Jackson Hole Board, and a few steering/stakeholder committees in Teton County Wyoming. He is on the Rendezvous Lands Conservancy board through his Emeritus status with the Jackson Hole Land Trust.">
          <div class="team-preview__card-image">
            <img src="/assets/images/about/team/scott-pierson.webp" alt="Scott Pierson, Board Chair of Community Foundation of Teton Valley" loading="lazy">
          </div>
          <div class="team-preview__card-info">
            <h3 class="team-preview__card-name">Scott Pierson</h3>
            <p class="team-preview__card-role">Board Chair</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="team-preview__card" role="button" tabindex="0" data-bio="Muffy Mead grew up on a cattle ranch in Jackson, Wyoming, but has spent her professional career in other cities. She is the author of the western memoir Its Head Came Off by Accident, and also wrote the best-selling Confessions of a Slacker Mom and Confessions of a Slacker Wife.||She is the CEO and founder of Nush Foods, a director of the M Lazy M Foundation, a member of the University of Utah's National Advisory Council, and a trustee at Westminster University.||She and her husband Scott Kauf reside in Alta, Wyoming, and Salt Lake City, Utah. As a member of Donor Relations, Muffy stresses, &quot;A Community Foundation is the ideal way to raise and distribute funds within rural areas. I have long admired how well our Foundation functions and the critical support it provides for such a wide range of deserving nonprofits throughout Teton Valley.&quot;">
          <div class="team-preview__card-image">
            <img src="/assets/images/about/team/muffy-mead.webp" alt="Muffy Mead, Vice Chair of Community Foundation of Teton Valley" loading="lazy">
          </div>
          <div class="team-preview__card-info">
            <h3 class="team-preview__card-name">Muffy Mead</h3>
            <p class="team-preview__card-role">Vice Chair</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="team-preview__card" role="button" tabindex="0" data-bio="Dean bought his first home in the valley in 1992 and moved here permanently in 2003 (with a hiatus in Jackson). He and his wife now live in Victor.||After 28 years of providing financial, tax, and investment advice to families and individuals, Dean sold his practice to begin a second career as a trumpet player. He can be seen playing in many area groups, crossing several genres. He hopes to be a prodigy by age 70.||Dean is also a current board member of the Idaho Falls Symphony and past board member of many musical and conservation nonprofits, including board emeritus for the Teton Regional Land Trust. He looks forward to helping promote the inclusive community approach that the Community Foundation espouses and aiding local nonprofits elevate their missions.">
          <div class="team-preview__card-image">
            <img src="/assets/images/about/team/dean-scofield.webp" alt="Dean Scofield, Treasurer and Finance Chair of Community Foundation of Teton Valley" loading="lazy">
          </div>
          <div class="team-preview__card-info">
            <h3 class="team-preview__card-name">Dean Scofield</h3>
            <p class="team-preview__card-role">Treasurer & Finance Chair</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="team-preview__card" role="button" tabindex="0" data-bio="Thad grew up and lived in the New York City area. He has been coming to the Teton Valley on ski vacations for more than 30 years. Four years ago, he and his partner Jeri bought a home here and fell in love with the scenic beauty, non-winter activities, and community the valley offers.||Thad spent most of his career helping businesses identify, assess, and manage the risks of their operations to make their businesses safer and more profitable. He recently retired as the director of a risk management advisory service for a large public corporation.||Thad first became involved with the Foundation by participating on the organization's grants committee. &quot;I think that the next few years will be a time of excitement and change for the Community Foundation, and I look forward to being able to help the organization continue to grow and succeed.&quot;">
          <div class="team-preview__card-image">
            <img src="/assets/images/about/team/thad-nosal.webp" alt="Thad Nosal, Secretary of Community Foundation of Teton Valley" loading="lazy">
          </div>
          <div class="team-preview__card-info">
            <h3 class="team-preview__card-name">Thad Nosal</h3>
            <p class="team-preview__card-role">Secretary</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="team-preview__card" role="button" tabindex="0" data-bio="Stella grew up in Tuscaloosa, Alabama, attended Sweet Briar College in Virginia, and graduated from the University of Alabama. Stella has an entrepreneurial spirit — she has created companies, products, and services all over the world.||She is currently the owner and designer of Bellemonde, a luggage and travel accessory company, and the CEO of Mini Many Memories, a custom keepsake Christmas ornament company. In addition to serving on the Board of the Community Foundation, she is active at St. John's Episcopal Church and is a member of the City of Victor volunteer Event Committee.||Tom and Stella followed their son to the Tetons beginning a decade ago. Stella says, &quot;We must have done something right in this life, to be so lucky to call this home!&quot;">
          <div class="team-preview__card-image">
            <img src="/assets/images/about/team/stella-martin.webp" alt="Stella Martin, Development and Outreach Chair of Community Foundation of Teton Valley" loading="lazy">
          </div>
          <div class="team-preview__card-info">
            <h3 class="team-preview__card-name">Stella Martin</h3>
            <p class="team-preview__card-role">Development & Outreach Chair</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="team-preview__card" role="button" tabindex="0" data-bio="Jeannette was born in the Republic of Panama where she lived and worked for the Department of Defense until transferring to the Pentagon in 1993. She worked in the Federal Government for more than 30 years in several executive positions including auditor for the Government Accountability Office and budget director in the U.S. Department of Agriculture.||Following Federal service, Jeannette worked for the MITRE Corporation, a not-for-profit corporation, for more than 10 years focusing on national security issues.||She has used her extensive management and financial experience to support the communities where she lives by volunteering in various nonprofit organizations. Jeannette and her husband Bill Horn built a home in Tetonia in 2013. &quot;It is a real privilege to be on the board of the Community Foundation of Teton Valley which works to improve the lives of everyone in our community.&quot;">
          <div class="team-preview__card-image">
            <img src="/assets/images/about/team/jeannette-chiari.webp" alt="Jeannette Chiari, Board Member of Community Foundation of Teton Valley" loading="lazy">
          </div>
          <div class="team-preview__card-info">
            <h3 class="team-preview__card-name">Jeannette Chiari</h3>
            <p class="team-preview__card-role">Board Member</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="team-preview__card" role="button" tabindex="0" data-bio="Ben was born and raised on Vancouver Island, British Columbia, and spent most of his adult life serving in the Canadian Army in a fulfilling occupation that took him worldwide.||In grad school, he met a girl from Jackson, and after attempting (poorly) to split time between Canada and the US for a few years, he decided to pop the question, retire, and call the Teton Valley home permanently.||After leaving the military, one of the aspects that Ben wanted to prioritize in his life was to become an active member of the community. He found an opportunity by volunteering with the Community Foundation and Food for Good Teton Valley, among others. When not doing that, he can be found chasing elk around the woods, skiing on Teton Pass, or exploring the amazing mountains that he feels blessed to enjoy living in.">
          <div class="team-preview__card-image">
            <img src="/assets/images/about/team/ben-turner.webp" alt="Ben Turner, Board Member of Community Foundation of Teton Valley" loading="lazy">
          </div>
          <div class="team-preview__card-info">
            <h3 class="team-preview__card-name">Ben Turner</h3>
            <p class="team-preview__card-role">Board Member</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="team-preview__card" role="button" tabindex="0" data-bio="Marie grew up on a ranch in northern California but spent much of her career working with clients in the San Francisco Bay Area, the Pacific Northwest, and East Coast. She retired in 2023 after more than 20 years directing her human resources consulting practice.||Marie is currently on the HOA Master Board of Teton Springs, is a CASA volunteer, and is committed to promoting our valley through philanthropy. She believes board members serve at the pleasure of the constituents they represent.||Marie, her husband Richard, and their dog Rex relocated to Teton Valley from Park City, Utah, five years ago to live in Victor. When Marie isn't busy gardening or cooking for friends and family, you can find her enjoying the outdoors, hiking with her dog, fishing, and traveling with her husband.">
          <div class="team-preview__card-image">
            <img src="/assets/images/about/team/marie-zolezzi.webp" alt="Marie Zolezzi, Board Member of Community Foundation of Teton Valley" loading="lazy">
          </div>
          <div class="team-preview__card-info">
            <h3 class="team-preview__card-name">Marie Zolezzi</h3>
            <p class="team-preview__card-role">Board Member</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="team-preview__card" role="button" tabindex="0" data-bio="Eileen grew up in Louisville, Kentucky, and studied economics as an undergraduate at Indiana University (go Hoosiers!). She spent two years at Wharton Econometric Forecasting Associates before attending Stanford Law School, where she met her husband, Gerard. She learned the importance of pro bono service starting with a work-study job at a community legal clinic during law school. Following graduation, she and Gerard considered a big-firm legal practice in Chicago and ended up staying in the area for 40 years.||Eileen spent 25 of those years practicing law full and part-time in various capacities, primarily in corporate transaction and compliance positions. Over the course of her professional career, she had the opportunity to continue pro bono legal work in areas including foreclosure mediation and guardianship of minors. She served a three-year term on the IRS Taxpayer Advocacy Panel, a federal advisory committee that serves as a liaison between the IRS and individual and small-business taxpayers. She also held numerous volunteer board positions in the school systems where she and Gerard raised their three children.||Eileen retired in 2021, and Gerard is semi-retired, so they now spend summers and winters at the house they built in Tetonia in 2012. Like so many, they take advantage of the beautiful outdoors around them by hiking, biking, skiing, and snowshoeing. As much as they like it in Teton Valley, they also enjoy travel, both domestic and international, especially expeditions to Boise to visit their grandchildren. Eileen is honored to serve on the board of the Community Foundation of Teton Valley, an organization that supports so many in the valley while exercising prudent stewardship of the resources entrusted to it.">
          <div class="team-preview__card-image">
            <img src="/assets/images/about/team/eileen-kelly.webp" alt="Eileen Kelly, Board Member of Community Foundation of Teton Valley" loading="lazy">
          </div>
          <div class="team-preview__card-info">
            <h3 class="team-preview__card-name">Eileen Kelly</h3>
            <p class="team-preview__card-role">Board Member</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="team-preview__card" role="button" tabindex="0" data-bio="September grew up in Pocatello, Idaho, and is a member of the Shoshone Bannock Tribes. She moved to Teton Valley in 2010, where she now lives full-time in Victor, ID.||She brings more than 40 years of experience in compliance, planning, permitting, and environmental conservation and consulting. She has 20+ years of experience as the Chief Executive Officer and founder of Sundance Consulting, Inc., a small, women-owned Native American business. She sold Sundance (95 employees) in 2024 and is happily retired.||September was introduced to the Community Foundation as a grants committee member in 2024. She is excited about the Community Foundation's thoughtful move toward independence and is eager to support the transition wherever needed. September and her husband, Shawn McFarland, love spending time with their blended families and enjoy skiing, rock climbing, biking, hiking, camping, and traveling abroad.">
          <div class="team-preview__card-image">
            <img src="/assets/images/about/team/september-myres.webp" alt="September Myres, Board Member of Community Foundation of Teton Valley" loading="lazy">
          </div>
          <div class="team-preview__card-info">
            <h3 class="team-preview__card-name">September Myres</h3>
            <p class="team-preview__card-role">Board Member</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="team-preview__card" role="button" tabindex="0" data-bio="Cathy grew up in Woodbury, NY, on Long Island, and moved West in 2001, first to Park City, Utah, and then to Victor in 2005, following a banking career in New York City.||Her first endeavor in Teton Valley was launching Music on Main in 2006 as the Teton Valley Foundation's first executive director. After the event's second season, she was asked to become the inaugural executive director of the Community Foundation of Teton Valley, with a charge to create the valley's first dedicated fundraising event for local nonprofits. The first Tin Cup Challenge took place on July 19, 2008.||In 2011, Cathy joined City Pass, Inc., a Victor-based company. She has been a Tin Cup Community Challenger since the event's inception in 2008. Cathy &quot;values the role the Foundation plays in fostering a collaborative, efficient, and resilient nonprofit community.&quot;">
          <div class="team-preview__card-image">
            <img src="/assets/images/about/team/cathy-oconnor.webp" alt="Cathy O'Connor, Board Member of Community Foundation of Teton Valley" loading="lazy">
          </div>
          <div class="team-preview__card-info">
            <h3 class="team-preview__card-name">Cathy O'Connor</h3>
            <p class="team-preview__card-role">Board Member</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="team-preview__card" role="button" tabindex="0" data-bio="In January 2018, Natalie Shirley was selected as the first female President and CEO of the National Cowboy &amp; Western Heritage Museum in Oklahoma City. Prior to that, she concurrently served as president of Oklahoma State University-Oklahoma City and as Governor Mary Fallin's Oklahoma Secretary of Education and Workforce Development.||From 2007-2011, she served in Governor Brad Henry's Cabinet as Oklahoma Secretary of Commerce and Tourism, responsible for the Workforce department and liaison between the governor, five major state agencies, and more than 30 small agencies.||She graduated from Oklahoma State University and earned a law degree from the University of Oklahoma. Shirley is married to Bill Schraegel and has six children. &quot;I am so excited and privileged to be part of the Community Foundation of Teton Valley. I believe it is important to participate in your community with your time, treasure, and talents.&quot;">
          <div class="team-preview__card-image">
            <img src="/assets/images/about/team/natalie-shirley.webp" alt="Natalie Shirley, Board Member of Community Foundation of Teton Valley" loading="lazy">
          </div>
          <div class="team-preview__card-info">
            <h3 class="team-preview__card-name">Natalie Shirley</h3>
            <p class="team-preview__card-role">Board Member</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="team-preview__card" role="button" tabindex="0" data-bio="Gene grew up in a suburb on the south side of Chicago and has a BS in Finance from DePaul University. During his 20 year career, Gene worked with several group health insurance companies.||Early on in Gene's career, he decided a skiing sabbatical was in order. This is when he discovered and fell in love with the Tetons. Not willing to live in a garage or out of his car, Gene returned to Chicago after three years to work and save for a permanent life in the mountains. That time came in February 2011 when he and his wife, Jenny, retired to Teton Valley permanently.||Gene is making up for a misspent youth and young adulthood by giving back to our Teton Valley Community. In addition to his Community Foundation board service, Gene also sits on the board of Teton Valley Trails and Pathways, and Teton County Idaho Search and Rescue. When not volunteering, Gene can be found mountain biking, hiking, on one of his many pairs of skis, or at the Pub usually with his dog, Darly.">
          <div class="team-preview__card-image">
            <img src="/assets/images/about/team/gene-marcowka.webp" alt="Gene Marcowka, Board Member Emeritus of Community Foundation of Teton Valley" loading="lazy">
          </div>
          <div class="team-preview__card-info">
            <h3 class="team-preview__card-name">Gene Marcowka</h3>
            <p class="team-preview__card-role">Emeritus</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

